<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>. ValidationRule.Description is
        capped at 255 characters; a comment is repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata
        API. It must sit INSIDE the root element. A comment placed ABOVE <ValidationRule>
        breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml
        file" error.

        =====================================================================================
        ADDED 2026-08-20 (Tranche 2, Workstream A1). THE FIRST VALIDATION RULE ON THIS OBJECT.
        =====================================================================================
        An offer with no offeror cannot be countered, compared or selected. Buyer identity is
        what DispositionApprovalService.selectOffer is ultimately choosing between.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 THIS RULE TARGETS Buyer_Name__c (TEXT) DELIBERATELY, AND WORKSTREAM D WILL
        RE-POINT IT. DO NOT READ THE TEXT FIELD AS AN OVERSIGHT.
        =====================================================================================
        Today the ONLY buyer field on this object is Buyer_Name__c, a Text(255) labelled
        "Buyer". Tranche 2 Workstream D adds Buyer__c, a Contact lookup, and makes it the
        entry point; Buyer_Name__c then becomes the DERIVED text stamped from it by
        DispositionOfferBuyerStampService and is NOT retired (requirements doc §5.4).

        ⇒ WHEN D LANDS, AMEND THIS ONE FILE: the formula becomes ISBLANK(Buyer__c) and
        errorDisplayField becomes Buyer__c. Amend, do not add a second rule, and do not leave
        both clauses in an OR: once Buyer_Name__c is derived, requiring it is requiring the
        stamp service to have run, which is not a data quality statement about anything the
        user did.

        WHY NOT DEFER THE WHOLE RULE TO D INSTEAD. Because analysts type Buyer_Name__c today
        and a blank one is wrong today. Requiring the field that EXISTS delivers the value
        now and costs one formula line later; the alternative delays half of A1 to the last
        tranche.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 WHY A RULE AND NOT `required=true`, WHICH IS THE SAME ANSWER AS ITS THREE SIBLINGS
        BUT FOR AN ADDITIONAL REASON HERE.
        =====================================================================================
        The three general reasons are in Broker_Required_On_Submission's header (delete
        constraint; a required field cannot carry FLS and both disposition permission sets
        would lose the grant; an authored message beats the platform's generic one).
        THE EXTRA REASON HERE IS THE FIELD SWAP ABOVE: `required=true` on Buyer_Name__c would
        have to be un set on live data and re set on the lookup in D, which is two schema
        changes on a field five consumers read. A rule is one file amended in place.

        =====================================================================================
        NO ISCHANGED / ISNEW GUARD. Invariant, not transition. Self clearing: the remedy,
        naming the buyer, is itself a permitted save.
        =====================================================================================
        MEASURED IMPACT AT CREATION: ZERO ROWS. Queried on usman-dpeg, 2026-08-20:
          SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Disposition_Offer__c                          -> 0
          SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Disposition_Offer__c WHERE Buyer_Name__c = null -> 0
        This rule refuses nothing that exists. 🔴 That measurement ages; re-run at deploy time.
        ⚠ TestDataFactory.createDispositionOffers ALREADY sets Buyer_Name__c and
        Offer_Amount__c, so neither A1 offer rule needs a factory change TODAY. That changes
        in D, when the required field becomes the lookup the factory does not set.
    -->
    <fullName>Buyer_Required_On_Offer</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>An offer must name who made it. Targets the Text field Buyer_Name__c because that is the only buyer field today; Workstream D adds a Buyer Contact lookup and this same rule file is amended to require the lookup instead. See the XML comment in this file.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>ISBLANK(Buyer_Name__c)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorMessage>Enter the Buyer who made this offer. An offer with no buyer cannot be countered, compared against the other offers, or selected as the winning offer.</errorMessage>
    <errorDisplayField>Buyer_Name__c</errorDisplayField>
</ValidationRule>
